module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.shared_symbol_projection_is_not_injective

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data shared_symbol_projection_is_not_injective: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "shared_symbol_projection_is_not_injective" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "shared symbol projection is not injective (A NAME-TO-SYMBOL PROJECTION SHARED BY EVERY TARGET ERASES A DISTINCTION THE SOURCE CARRIED, and nothing refuses, so two distinct identities silently become one emitted symbol. ",

    "THE INVALID STATE is two distinct authored identities that project to one emitted symbol. The harm is that the second definition overwrites or shadows the first in the emitted artifact and the program still compiles: a wrong artifact with NO diagnostic, which is the silent-wrongness DESIGN.md section 5 places outside the ladder entirely. ",

    "RECEIPT, observed rather than argued: `sanitize_service_name` splits the authored name on '.' and joins the capitalized segments with nothing, so the segment boundary is erased. Two services named `collision.Probe` and `CollisionProbe` in one module emitted two `pub struct CollisionProbe` definitions and bound one parameter for both, with zero blocking diagnostics. `service_var_name` is the second channel, since to_snake of one symbol is one symbol. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder -- silent wrongness, not rung 1, because no arm fires at all. The sibling projection at the same grain, `module_to_filename`, is at rung 1: it maps '.' to '_' and is equally many-to-one, but `module_filename_collision_diagnostics` refuses on the collision and all three emitters call it. So the shape of the remedy is already in the corpus; what is missing is the instance. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: when a projection from authored names to emitted symbols DELETES a separator rather than escaping it, it is many-to-one, and the question is not whether a collision is likely but whether anything observes one. Grep the projection's call sites: if every one of them consumes the result directly and none of them folds the whole population first, there is no observer and the collision is silent. ",

    "WHY THE WALL DID NOT LAND WITH THE ROW, stated so the gap is not read as an oversight: the refusal needs its own CompilerDiagnostic variant, and that coproduct's seed projection is a hand-maintained receipt row that gunbc#10688 declares FROZEN. Landing the variant there would have one commit declare a freeze and breach it. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMED AS A CAPABILITY AND NOT AS A MERGE (section 4b(3)): a typed CompilerDiagnostic receipt carrier existing -- a carrier from which the seed's exhaustiveness obligation is derived rather than hand-counted -- at which point adding a diagnostic variant no longer edits a frozen figure and the collision fold lands beside `module_filename_collision_diagnostics` in the shape that already works. A trigger naming one pull request would be satisfied while the capability stayed dead if that lane were superseded. ",

    "ATTAINABLE CEILING: rung 2 by the same route as the filename collision -- the population is a fold over the emitted service set and the refusal is decidable, but the invalid state stays WRITABLE in source, so structural impossibility would need an allocation whose distinct identities cannot share a symbol by construction. That allocation is not proposed here. ",

    "WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED: this row does not claim the collision has occurred in the live corpus. The receipt is a constructed fixture. The claim is that nothing would report it if it did.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
